From 627c10779ba2fffdd3215f744901d8606ccc7c07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:09:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: add per-frame audio-pump-loop timing diagnostic

Real 486DX2-50 data from the render-loop diagnostic (patch 0010) came
back: fps holds at ~3.04 (vs. 3.15 before that patch -- within noise,
consistent with the small 100x12 viewport / 2-animation scene weakening
the sprite-scan hypothesis as predicted). Real frame time is ~329ms
(54s / 164 frames). Render loop itself measured ~63.5-77ms/loop
steady-state (first sample 113ms, likely warm-up/cache effects,
excluded). Combined with the SDL3-DOS backend's own flush-timing
instrumentation (~50ms/flush, confirmed constant across builds by an
earlier vcctrl cross-build comparison), that's only ~120-190ms of the
~329ms frame time accounted for -- still a ~140-200ms/frame gap.

Leading remaining candidate, not yet measured directly: the per-frame
audio-ring pump loop itself (game.cpp, patch 0007/0008), bounded to at
most 4 SDL_DOSAudioPump() calls/frame by patch 0008's iteration cap.
That cap was sized to bound worst-case cost assuming per-call cost was
modest -- but the original real-hardware finding that motivated the cap
(SDLDBG.LOG showing SDL_DOSAudioPump repeatedly hitting its own
>32-iteration safety counter) was never converted into a direct
per-call wall-clock measurement on this specific CPU. 4 calls at
roughly the same magnitude as a single video flush (~50ms) would
account for almost exactly the remaining gap.

Adds a temporary diagnostic (__DJGPP__-guarded, mirrors patch 0010's
RENDERDBG.LOG pattern): times the whole bounded pump loop (not
individual SDL_DOSAudioPump() calls -- the loop already exits early
whenever the ring reaches target depth, so total loop time already
reflects real per-frame cost) and logs avg ms + avg iteration count to
PUMPDBG.LOG every 20 frames.

Verified under DOSBox-X: builds, boots, plays normally, PUMPDBG.LOG
populates. No behavior change -- purely additive logging alongside the
existing pump loop. Real-hardware measurement on the 486DX2-50 is the
next step, to confirm or rule out the audio pump loop as the dominant
remaining per-frame cost.
---
 gameSource/game.cpp | 40 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gameSource/game.cpp b/gameSource/game.cpp
index e0acf33..3ca3255 100644
--- a/gameSource/game.cpp
+++ b/gameSource/game.cpp
@@ -1101,11 +1101,51 @@ char playGame() {
                 pumpClampedTargetMs = pumpCapacityMs;
                 }
             int pumpIters = 0;
+
+            // TEMPORARY DIAGNOSTIC (PUMPDBG.LOG): the render-loop cost
+            // diagnostic (RENDERDBG.LOG, patch 0010) plus the SDL3-DOS
+            // backend's own flush-timing instrumentation (~50ms/flush,
+            // constant across builds) only accounted for ~120ms of the
+            // ~325ms real 486DX2-50 average frame time -- this bounded
+            // pump loop (capped at 4 iterations by patch 0008) is the
+            // remaining candidate: if each SDL_DOSAudioPump() call costs
+            // real wall-clock time proportional to CPU speed rather than
+            // audio-time produced (as hypothesized in the comment above,
+            // never directly measured), 4 calls could plausibly explain
+            // the remaining ~200ms gap on its own. Time the whole loop
+            // directly rather than assuming.
+            double pumpLoopStartTime = Time::getCurrentTime();
+
             while( pumpIters < pumpMaxIters &&
                    SDL_DOSAudioRingFillMs() < pumpClampedTargetMs &&
                    SDL_DOSAudioPump() ) {
                 pumpIters ++;
                 }
+
+            {
+                double pumpLoopElapsed = Time::getCurrentTime() - pumpLoopStartTime;
+                static double pumpLoopElapsedTotal = 0;
+                static int pumpLoopItersTotal = 0;
+                static int pumpLoopFrameCount = 0;
+                pumpLoopElapsedTotal += pumpLoopElapsed;
+                pumpLoopItersTotal += pumpIters;
+                pumpLoopFrameCount ++;
+                if( pumpLoopFrameCount >= 20 ) {
+                    FILE *pumpLog = fopen( "PUMPDBG.LOG", "a" );
+                    if( pumpLog != NULL ) {
+                        fprintf( pumpLog,
+                                 "[pump-loop-cost n=%d] avg_ms=%f "
+                                 "avg_iters=%f\n",
+                                 pumpLoopFrameCount,
+                                 1000.0 * pumpLoopElapsedTotal / pumpLoopFrameCount,
+                                 (double)pumpLoopItersTotal / pumpLoopFrameCount );
+                        fclose( pumpLog );
+                        }
+                    pumpLoopElapsedTotal = 0;
+                    pumpLoopItersTotal = 0;
+                    pumpLoopFrameCount = 0;
+                    }
+                }
             }
 #endif
 
